From a1887ce920f2155ed07c3020ac2d1c5054ad6a5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tanzeel Khan <tzlkhan@amazon.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:51:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix engine build with GCC 15 (C23 default)

GCC 15 compiles C as C23 by default, where an empty parameter list
"()" means "(void)" instead of "unspecified parameters". The
pltsql_is_partitioned_table_reloptions_allowed_hook typedef was
declared with "()" but is called with the reloptions Datum, so
reloptions.c failed to compile:

  error: too many arguments to function
  'pltsql_is_partitioned_table_reloptions_allowed_hook'; expected 0,
  have 1

Declare the hook with its real (Datum reloptions) parameter, and give
the other Babelfish hook typedefs that take no arguments an explicit
(void) so they are proper prototypes on every C standard.

Also stop removeTimeZoneStrFromTypmod() from writing through a
const char * it got from strstr(); with C23 and glibc 2.43 strstr()
returns a const pointer for const input, which made this a
-Wdiscarded-qualifiers warning. Its only caller passes a palloc'd
buffer.

Task: BABEL-7211
Signed-off-by: Tanzeel Khan <tzlkhan@amazon.com>
---
 src/backend/utils/adt/format_type.c | 2 +-
 src/include/access/attmap.h         | 2 +-
 src/include/access/reloptions.h     | 2 +-
 src/include/catalog/namespace.h     | 2 +-
 src/include/commands/sequence.h     | 2 +-
 src/include/utils/builtins.h        | 2 +-
 6 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/utils/adt/format_type.c b/src/backend/utils/adt/format_type.c
index 7f245ac6724..d94f16e063b 100644
--- a/src/backend/utils/adt/format_type.c
+++ b/src/backend/utils/adt/format_type.c
@@ -365,7 +365,7 @@ format_type_with_typemod(Oid type_oid, int32 typemod)
 }
 
 static void
-removeTimeZoneStrFromTypmod(const char *tmstr, const char *tzstr)
+removeTimeZoneStrFromTypmod(char *tmstr, const char *tzstr)
 {
 	char *substr = strstr(tmstr, tzstr);
 	if (substr)
